BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:January Movie Screening- At Eternity's Gate ﻿﻿
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270125T200000
UID:6afcb926d7e98e002c537cc4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the last Monday of every month for a special screen
 ing celebrating the best in cinema! We’ll be featuring acclaimed films c
 reated by Academy Award winners and nominees. Grab a seat\, settle in\, an
 d enjoy a great movie with fellow film lovers.\nDrop in!\nJanuary feature:
  At Eternity's Gate- 1hr 51min\nAcademy Award® nominee Julian Schnabel's
  AT ETERNITY'S GATE is a journey inside the world and mind of a person who
 \, despite skepticism\, ridicule and illness\, created some of the world's
  most beloved and stunning works of art. This is not a forensic biography\
 , but rather scenes based on Vincent van Gogh's (Academy Award® nominee W
 illem Dafoe) letters\, common agreement about events in his life that pres
 ent as facts\, hearsay\, and moments that are just plain invented.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afcb926d7e98e002c537cc4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270203T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270203T170000
UID:6ae39eb0901b02002cc6034e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae39eb0901b02002cc6034e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senior's E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270119T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270119T173000
UID:6a56c066fb418a28009b035f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you have questions about your tablet\, phone\, laptop\, ema
 il or an app?  Need help with eBooks or other online library services? We
  can help!\nJoin us for this intergenerational program that pairs teen vol
 unteers with seniors to answer your tech questions.\nDrop in\, no registra
 tion is required. Participants may be limited to 1/2 hr sessions.\nEvery T
 uesday\, from 4:00-5:30 pm. Please note\, sessions will not run on Decembe
 r 15th\, December 22nd and December 29th\, but will resume on January 5th\
 , 2027.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a56c066fb418a28009b035f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult & Senior's Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T153000
UID:6b01c89cd164f314d93d4136@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our adult and senior’s social as we engage in va
 rious activities\, games and crafts. Relax\, have fun\, and learn somethin
 g new while connecting with new friends.\nThis is a drop-in program.\nActi
 vities for December:\nMonday\, December 7 - Film Screening: Christmas Holi
 days (1944 Film)\nMonday\, December 14 - Collage\n*Please note there will 
 be no programs on Monday\, December 21\, and Monday\, December 28*
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b01c89cd164f314d93d4136
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chess For Life: Seniors Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261209T143000
UID:6ada61c7377296003a4dd6c1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Chess Institute of Canada invites you to join our Chess fo
 r Life program — a fun and engaging chess program for seniors of all ski
 ll levels.\nWhether you are a seasoned player or new to the game\, enjoy f
 riendly matches\, sharpen your strategy\, and connect with others in a rel
 axed\, supportive environment.\nCome make your move!\nRegistration require
 d.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada61c7377296003a4dd6c1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
