BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Weston Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270227T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270227T110000
UID:6afc85b7d7e98e002c536909@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of Black History Month\, join us for a lively d
 iscussion of Cynthia Erivo’s\nSimply More\n.\nThis memoir explores theme
 s of self-acceptance\, personal growth\, and resilience. Through a series 
 of vulnerable vignettes\, Erivo reflects on her life\, her career as an ac
 tor and the lessons she has learned along the way—offering encouragement
  to anyone who has ever felt marginalized\, hyper-visible\, or told they t
 ake up too much space.\nDrop-In. No Registration Required.\nLight Refreshm
 ents Served.
LOCATION:Weston\, Youth Hub Area\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afc85b7d7e98e002c536909
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
