BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Retirement Planning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T153000
UID:69fcdc91f6bd012f006661cd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Riverdale Immigrant Women's Centre\, this worksho
 p is an introduction to long-term financial planning including retirement 
 savings and better understanding of federal income benefits\, such as\, Ca
 nada Pension Plan (CPP) and Old Age Security (OAS).\nDrop in.
LOCATION:Parliament Street
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fcdc91f6bd012f006661cd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270217T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270217T170000
UID:6ae39eb0901b02002cc60350@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae39eb0901b02002cc60350
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
