UID:6b01feab4ec0691f07afafcb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Using acrylic paints and colourful sand\, create your very own
  northern lights masterpiece that you can take home. All materials will be
  provided.\nSpace is limited. Tickets will be given out 30 minutes prior t
 o program start time.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b01feab4ec0691f07afafcb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Winter Light: The Memoir of a Child of Holocaust Survivors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270106T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270106T153000
UID:6b01fd3c4ec0691f07afafbe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Winter Light\n​ (Amsterdam Publishers\, 2024) is about a seq
 uence of serendipitous rescues—an emotional rags-to-riches story.\nGrace
  Feuerverger\, professor emerita of the University of Toronto\, will share
  her story of hope and gratitude which adds a radically different piece to
  the mosaic of post-Holocaust literature. At the core of her memoir stands
  a little girl struggling to find a path toward the Life force and to esca
 pe from the demons of despair that permeated her home.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6b01fd3c4ec0691f07afafbe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adult Afternoon Movie - Is This Thing On? (2025)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T160000
UID:6ab2cc01001a4a0e055b355c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As their marriage quietly unravels\, Alex (Will Arnett) faces
  middle age and an impeding divorce\, seeking new purpose in the New York
  comedy scene while\, his wife Tess (Laura Dern) confronts sacrifices mad
 e for their family\, forcing them to navigate co-parenting\, identity\, an
 d whether love can take a new form.\nR\, 121 minutes\n**Subtitles for the 
 deaf and hard of hearing when available (SDH).
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2cc01001a4a0e055b355c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
