BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Afternoon Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261214T140000
UID:6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7948@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the following Monday afternoons to discuss books i
 n a friendly and social atmosphere: September 14th\, October 19th\, Novemb
 er 9th\, and December 14th.\nThis month we will be reading\nThe MANIAC\nby
  Benjamin Labatut.\nThe MANIAC\nis a 2023 novel by Chilean author Benjami
 n Labatut\, and his first in English (compared to his usual Spanish). It 
 is a fictionalized biography of polymath John von Neumann interwoven with 
 tripartite narratives exploring the intersection of human genius\, ration
 ality\, and artificial intelligence. Told via oral-history style from peer
 s\, wives\, and colleagues\, Labatut attempts to decipher core themes of r
 eason and madness\, the edge of progress\, and the loss of the sacred. Wh
 ile a spiritual sequel to\nWhen We Cease to Understand the World\n\,\nno p
 rior knowledge of science or technology is needed to appreciate Labatut's 
 polymathic portrait of von Neumann.\nParticipants can borrow a copy of the
  book from the Woodside Square branch upon registration.\nInformation Coll
 ection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the 
 Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 2
 0(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program 
 registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library ha
 ndles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@
 tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7948
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
