BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Love Will Out-A Newfoundland Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270223T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270223T150000
UID:6afe082ac58b38184c0789e8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:David Michael presents\, 'Love Will Out'\, a novel based on hi
 s parents very unusual love story in St. John's\, NL\, during the 1920s a
 nd 30s -- twenty years before Newfoundland joined Canada.\nDavid's father 
 was Maronite Christian Lebanese and mother was Polish Jewish. Their story 
 begins in Poland and Lebanon recounting the reasons why David's grandpare
 nts left their respective countries and emigrated to Newfoundland. It cont
 inues on to their children (David's parents) and how they discovered eac
 h other and fell in love.\nRegistration required.\nInformation Collection 
 Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6afe082ac58b38184c0789e8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
