BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scam Protection For Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261215T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261215T153000
UID:6b077821cee779003a30041a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Build confidence and learn how to protect your personal inform
 ation in this free\, staff-led workshop for older adults. Using plain-lang
 uage\, real-world examples\, library staff will show you how to spot red f
 lags and stay safe from today's most common frauds. Bring your questions f
 or an open Q&A in a welcoming\, judgment-free setting.\nWhat we will cover
 :\nPhone & text scams:\nSpotting fake bank alerts\, government impersonato
 rs\, and urgent "emergency" calls\nAI voice cloning:\nRecognizing how scam
 mers mimic familiar voices and setting up a family safe-word\nEmail & onli
 ne shopping fraud:\nIdentifying fake delivery notices\, phishing links\, a
 nd unsafe websites\nPasswords & privacy:\nSimple ways to create strong pas
 swords and lock down your account settings\nProgram Details:\nAudience:\nO
 lder adults and seniors (family members and caregivers welcome)\nCost:\nFr
 ee\nRegistration:\nRequired (space is limited)\nTakeaway:\nA printed quick
 -reference checklist of red flags and reporting resources (such as the Can
 adian Anti-Fraud Centre)\nRegistration is required.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview
